  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 237 PM MDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nSynoptically, the long term setup remains largely unchanged. The \nupper level flow will continue to be mainly zonal. As we move into \nthe weekend, Guidance is suggesting the ridge of the western US will \nbegin to re-amplify and propogate to the east. This will begin to \ntransition the flow to be from the northwest. During this period \nthere will be a few shortwaves that will move through the region \ncreating some precipitation chances. \n\nWednesday's high temperatures look to be the \"coolest\" of the \nperiod, with highs in the 80s to low 90s. A warming trend will \nbegin on Thursday, with highs in the mid to upper 90s. By Friday\nand Saturday, the majority of the CWA will see highs in the\nupper 90s. Also, some locations could see localized highs \nreaching triple digits. Winds look to remain calm to breezy \nthroughout mid week to the weekend. Relative humidity values are\nforecast to mainly stay above 20% except for Friday were \neastern Colorado could see values in the high teens to low 20s. \nMoving to precipitation, there is a 10-20% chance of \nshowers/storms each afternoon and evening as shortwaves move \nthrough the CWA.",
